Keep the old method and add an overloaded Optional-based variant. Example service signatures/implementation sketch:
1) public List<Task> listTasksForUser(Long userId) { return listTasksForUser(userId, Optional.empty()); }
2) public List<Task> listTasksForUser(Long userId, Optional<String> statusOpt) {
   if (statusOpt.isPresent()) {
     try {
       TaskStatus s = TaskStatus.valueOf(statusOpt.get());
       return repository.findByUserIdAndStatus(userId, s);
     } catch (IllegalArgumentException e) {
       return Collections.emptyList(); // unknown status -> no matches
     }
   }
   return repository.findByUserId(userId);
}
Controller change (call site):
- add @RequestParam(value = "status", required = false) String status and call taskService.listTasksForUser(userId, Optional.ofNullable(status)); This preserves existing callers, keeps current default behavior, and returns an empty list (200) for unknown status values.

